  "user_request_original": "Design a 30-layer chirped multilayer coating on SiO2 (Lemarchand) substrate with air incidence. Stack sequence: alternating hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) layers, starting with hfo2, for 30 total layers. Layer thicknesses follow a chirped progression where optical thickness varies systematically from layer 1 to layer 30 to cover 400-700 nm reflection band. Optimize the chirp parameter and individual layer thickness deviations to maximize reflectance uniformity in 400-700 nm and transmittance in 1530-1565 nm. Use measured refractive index data for hfo2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) from the material catalog. Total layer count fixed at 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a thirty-layer air/HfO2/SiO2/substrate chirped mirror optimizing layer thicknesses to maximize reflectance uniformity in 400–700 nm and transmittance in 1530–1565 nm, using registry-resolved material data and compiling a two percent relative thickness tolerance.",
